# --- Pronoun sets — sex/gender INDEPENDENT; custom sets fill the five forms -- #
# Canonical ANCHOR inventory of stably-declinable English pronoun sets (each with
# all five forms). The list is an exhaustive set of anchors, NOT a fence: a set not
# seeded here is expressed by minting a fresh gmeow:PronounSet filling the five
# forms (see test_custom_pronoun_set_has_five_forms). Declensions verified against
# the pronouns.page / Pronoun Dressing Room structured database (en.pronouns.page,
# the five morphemes pronoun_subject/object/possessive_determiner/possessive_pronoun/
# reflexive) and cross-checked with pronouns.within.lgbt; cf. docs/identity-mapping.md
# for the full sourcing note. The set aligns (where a target exists) to Wikidata's
# 'personal pronoun set' (wd:Q65067284) in mapping-dsl/equivalences/names.ttl.
gmeow:honorificSama skos:definition "The sama honorific — a term of respect, rank, or courtesy used when addressing or naming a person."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/names> .

gmeow:pronounSheHer a gmeow:PronounSet ; rdfs:label "she/her"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:pronounSubject "she" ; gmeow:pronounObject "her" ;
    gmeow:pronounPossessiveDeterminer "her" ; gmeow:pronounPossessive "hers" ;
    gmeow:pronounReflexive "herself" .
gmeow:pronounSheHer skos:definition "The she/her pronoun set — a third-person pronoun paradigm used to refer to an entity in discourse."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/names> .
